  "output": "The book follows a magitech artificer who takes a routine guild job in a ruin that is \"folded out of space and stuck in a single looping hour\" [1]. The story is set in the guild-city of Threnn, where magic is a \"shattered art tiered into Facets,\" some of which are forbidden or lost [4]. The plot involves a party taking a commission at \"the Nine,\" discovering something is wrong, and dealing with a loop, a survivor, and a \"Keystone\" [3].\n\nThe protagonist is Cael Ferren [2], [5]. She is a 26-year-old brass-rank artificer who has spent her life hiding the fact that she can feel the \"deep, forbidden Facets of magic\" [1], [2], [5]. While she initially desires a quiet, unremarkable career and believes her ability is a \"sickness,\" she eventually learns that this \"hum\" is actually a \"compass to a magic the world broke on purpose\" [5].",
